Owner decision 2026-09-02 ("待决策项以 rfidak.com 的口径为准"). 522 editorial
JSON files and 13 diagrams. Line-level changelog:
AUDIT_2026-09-01/phase14/B8-content-changelog.csv.
- D-04 production model: 'in-house / own factory / our lines / one roof /
  no subcontracting / factory-direct' wording (274 sentences in 75 files, 13
  SVG diagrams) rewritten to the rfidak model — Proud Tek owns the
  specification, chip sourcing and QC sign-off; tooling and production run
  on contracted partner lines to our spec; 'manufacturer-direct' replaces
  'factory-direct' as the sourcing term (URLs unchanged). /about/factory/
  rewritten around rfidak's 'who does what' table; /about/ summary, hero,
  capability sections and FAQ rewritten; the 'RFID factory direct' LP
  rewritten around specification ownership instead of machine ownership
- D-05 / D-09 commercial terms: 'firm quote in one business day' (103
  product briefs) -> 'written quote within 24-48 hours'; reply promises ->
  2-4 h in business hours; sample policy (2-3 SKUs / 5-20 pieces, 1 business
  day preparation, 3-6 days door-to-door, freight refunded against the first
  order, custom samples +3-5 days); MOQ statements (500 cards/keyfobs/
  wristbands, 1,000 tags/labels, stock 100, UHF inlays 5,000, custom
  tooling 2,000-5,000, halves after three orders); lead time 7-15 business
  days; payment 30/70, L/C or 50/50, PayPal < 00; wristband MOQ 200 -> 500
- D-06 bylines: authorSlug/author -> editorial-board / 'Proud Tek Editorial
  Team', reviewedBySlug/reviewedBy -> proudtek-engineering / 'Proud Tek RF /
  Production Engineering' on all 522 pages; /about/review-board/ and
  /about/leadership/ rewritten as function pages; remaining named mentions
  removed (editorial-policy, blog hub)
- K-11 / K-12 certificates: /about/certifications/ registry now lists
  OEKO-TEX 23.HCN.97349 (UHF laundry tag), RoHS XKS2025R01150076, REACH SVHC
  XKS2025R10150032E and CE/RED EN 62311 BCTC2509165308-1E with issuer,
  scope and validity; material-compliance wording is sample-based
- D-07: FeliCa / HITAG redirects unchanged — rfidak lists Hitag as a stocked
  LF family (no proudtek page exists) and does not list FeliCa
