   "title": "NFC vs Bluetooth — Short-Range Wireless Compared",
   "kicker": "NFC vs Bluetooth",
   "summary": "NFC and Bluetooth (including BLE) are both short-range wireless technologies built into nearly every modern smartphone, but they occupy fundamentally different ends of the proximity spectrum. NFC operates at contact distance (0-5 cm) for intentional tap-based interactions. Payments, access control, authentication, instant data exchange. Bluetooth Classic and BLE operate at 1-10 m and 10-100 m respectively for sustained data streaming. Audio, file transfer, IoT sensors, room-scale and building-scale presence. This comparison walks through the radio physics, data rates, security properties, pairing behavior and cost structure of each technology, and shows why the two are most often deployed together (NFC tap to initiate, Bluetooth to sustain) rather than as alternatives.",
